            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 9,
              "start": 9
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Benjamin J. Horwich, the attorneys\u2019\u2011fees provision looks to the judgment at the end of a case, not to the filing deadline, and therefore may apply even when a petition is filed late."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Benjamin J. Horwich",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Benjamin J. Horwich, petitioner argues that the Vaccine Act does not provide for an award of attorneys\u2019 fees when a petition is filed after the statutory deadline."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondent contends that Section\u202f15(e)(1) makes any petition eligible for fees if it is filed in good faith and with a reasonable basis, even when the petition is denied."
      }
    ],
