              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Sotomayor asked Mr. Horwich to elaborate on his argument regarding the fee provision."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg inquired about other provisions of the Act that refer to a petition\u2019s filing."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 7,
              "start": 7
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked about the reporting\u2011to\u2011Congress provision and whether it occurs at the beginning, middle, or end of a case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kennedy, justice Kennedy questioned whether filing means different things under different provisions of the Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether the attorneys\u2019\u2011fees provision, which looks to the end of the case, should be construed to apply to untimely filings."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor suggested that the argument sounded jurisdictional and noted the government\u2019s concession that the statute of limitations is not jurisdictional."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0000-0011"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, justice Alito presented an example where a timely petition failed on the merits but still raised the issue of fee eligibility."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, justice Sotomayor expressed confusion about whether an award of attorneys\u2019 fees on a good\u2011faith basis depends on the ultimate merits of the vaccine injury claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked how often claims are rejected solely on timeliness grounds."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kagan asked why untimely petitions usually arise, suggesting they often involve issues such as reporting requirements."
      }
    ],
