            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns whether the Vaccine Act\u2019s attorneys\u2019 fees provision applies to petitions that are denied as untimely."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Government",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0001-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 26
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Section\u202f15(e)(1) of the Vaccine Act allows an award of attorneys\u2019 fees when a petition is filed in good faith and with a reasonable basis, regardless of the petition\u2019s ultimate outcome."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d66524684df511663d51809360deee96342d2951944a5d18b12332d575d35dd",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d66524684df-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Over the past 25\u202fyears the vaccine injury program has paid roughly $160\u202fmillion in attorneys\u2019 fees to both winners and losers, representing about 6\u202fpercent of total compensation paid."
      }
    ],
